course: dictionary
lesson: 9979
title: Tease: friendly fun or unkind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To tease someone means to laugh at them or make jokes about them. To tease an animal means to annoy it on purpose. A person who likes to tease others is also called a tease. The same word can be friendly or unkind, so the context tells you which one it means.
explain: «Everyone can like what they like; teasing about interests makes people hide what they enjoy.» Here teasing is unkind, because it makes people feel they must hide the things they love. Ask yourself: does the teasing make everyone feel good, or does it make someone feel sad?
explain: «Just teasing!» is what someone says when they want you to know they did not mean it seriously. But if the teasing keeps going after you say stop, it is no longer a joke. Then say «Stop, I don't like that», walk away, and tell an adult.
fact: To tease means to laugh at someone or make jokes about them, in a friendly way or an unkind way.
fact: To tease an animal means to annoy it on purpose, such as poking it or waving food at it.
fact: A tease is a person who likes to tease others.
fact: Teasing an animal can make it angry, so it might bite or scratch.
fact: Friendly teasing is gentle and fun for both sides; teasing that hurts is unkind and can be bullying.
exercise: Ayesha says, «Just teasing!» What does she mean? | She is angry and will shout | *She did not mean it seriously | She wants a new pet | She is going to a party
exercise: «Poking the dog and waving food at it is teasing an animal.» What does tease mean for an animal? | To annoy it on purpose | *To annoy it on purpose, and it might bite | To give it a bath | To teach it new tricks
exercise: What is a tease? | *A person who likes to tease others | A small cake | A kind teacher | A type of animal
test: «If you are teased about your looks, say "Stop, I don't like that", walk away, and tell an adult if it continues.» What should you do if the teasing continues? | *Tell an adult | Laugh louder | Tease them back | Keep quiet and hope it stops
test: In «He will tease his friend about his new hat», what does tease mean if it is friendly? | To hug them | To run away | To cry | *To laugh at someone or make a joke about them
exam: Which kind of teasing is unkind? | Just teasing, said with a smile | *Teasing that makes someone feel sad or hurt | A joke that everyone laughs at together | Gentle teasing that both friends enjoy
